IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-interpretation`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-bedrooms`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-payments`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-contributions`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-private-sector`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 4 (housing costs element for renters): Part 5, the social rented sector.
-- Paragraphs 30 to 36 (including 32A).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text). Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Layer 1.
--
-- The element is amount S, less the housing cost contributions (paragraph 33). S is the monthly total of the relevant payments less any
-- under-occupation deduction (paragraph 34), or, for joint tenants, a share of that total (paragraph 35).
--
-- ORDER OF THE ADJUSTMENTS TO ONE PAYMENT (fork U3-F23, assumed and not ruled). Paragraphs 31, 32 and 32A each change the amount of a relevant
-- payment, and the text does not say in what order. The module reads them in the order of the sub-paragraphs' own logic: a tenant incentive
-- reduction is added back first (32A: "as if no such reduction had been applied"), then the amount that relates to a commodity is deducted (31),
-- and a rent officer's lower amount, if used, replaces the amount of the payment altogether (32(4): "instead of the amount of the relevant payment
-- for which the renter is liable").
--
-- UNDER-OCCUPATION WITH JOINT TENANTS (fork U3-F22). Paragraph 36(2) defines the amount of the deduction only for paragraph 34 and paragraph 35(3).
-- In a paragraph 35(4) or (5) case the text gives no deduction, and the module gives none, though paragraph 36(1) says a deduction "is to be made"
-- whenever the accommodation has more bedrooms than the renter is entitled to.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 30: Part 5 applies to a renter liable to make rent payments to a provider of social housing, whether or not also liable for service charges.
-- src:2528 | (1) This Part applies to renters who are liable to make rent payments to a provider of social housing.
-- src:2529 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1) applies irrespective of whether renters are also liable to make service charge payments.
@ref Sch 4 para 30 (src:2528-2529)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter whose landlord decides the Part`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 30 — Part 5 applies to the renter` renter MEANS
    `Sch 4 para 2 — provider of social housing` (renter's `the landlord that rent payments are payable to`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 32A(2): an approved tenant incentive scheme.
-- src:2542 | (2) In paragraph (1) “approved tenant incentive scheme” means a scheme which is—
-- src:2543 | (a) operated by a provider of social housing and designed to avoid rent arrears by allowing reductions in rent or service charges or other advantages in return for meeting specified conditions; and
-- src:2544 | (b) approved by the Secretary of State.
@ref Sch 4 para 32A(2) (src:2542-2544)
DECLARE `Tenant incentive scheme` HAS
    `the scheme is operated by a provider of social housing and designed to avoid rent arrears by allowing reductions in rent or service charges or other advantages in return for meeting specified conditions`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the scheme is approved by the Secretary of State`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2542 | (2) In paragraph (1) “approved tenant incentive scheme” means a scheme which is—
-- src:2543 | (a) operated by a provider of social housing and designed to avoid rent arrears by allowing reductions in rent or service charges or other advantages in return for meeting specified conditions; and
-- src:2544 | (b) approved by the Secretary of State.
@ref Sch 4 para 32A(2) (src:2542-2544)
GIVEN scheme IS A `Tenant incentive scheme`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 32A(2) — an approved tenant incentive scheme` scheme MEANS
    (scheme's `the scheme is operated by a provider of social housing and designed to avoid rent arrears by allowing reductions in rent or service charges or other advantages in return for meeting specified conditions`)
    AND (scheme's `the scheme is approved by the Secretary of State`)

-- One relevant payment in the social rented sector, with the facts that paragraphs 31, 32 and 32A adjust it by.
-- src:2531 | 31 Deduction from relevant payments of amounts relating to use of particular accommodation
-- src:2532 | In determining the amount of any relevant payment to be taken into account under paragraph 6, a deduction is to be made for any amount which the Secretary of State is satisfied—
-- src:2533 | (a) is included in the relevant payment; but
-- src:2534 | (b) relates to the supply to the accommodation of a commodity (such as water or fuel) for use by any member of the renter's extended benefit unit.
-- src:2535 | 32 Power to apply to rent officer if relevant payments excessive
-- src:2536 | (1) Sub-paragraph (2) applies where it appears to the Secretary of State that the amount of any relevant payment for which the renter is liable in respect of accommodation occupied by the renter is greater than it is reasonable to meet by way of the housing costs element under this Part.
-- src:2537 | (2) The Secretary of State may apply to a rent officer for a determination to be made as to the amount of the relevant payment by the officer in exercise of the officer's Housing Act functions.
-- src:2538 | (3) Sub-paragraph (4) applies in any case where a rent officer determines that a landlord might, at the time of the application under sub-paragraph (2), reasonably have expected to obtain a lower amount of the description of relevant payment referred to the rent officer.
-- src:2539 | (4) The lower amount determined by the rent officer is to be used in making the calculation under this Part, instead of the amount of the relevant payment for which the renter is liable, unless the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is not appropriate to use that lower amount.
-- src:2540 | 32A Reduction under tenant incentive scheme
-- src:2541 | (1) Where a reduction in the rent or service charge payments for which a renter would otherwise have been liable is applied by a provider of social housing under an approved tenant incentive scheme, the amount of any relevant payment to be taken into account under paragraph 6 is to be determined as if no such reduction had been applied.
-- src:2542 | (2) In paragraph (1) “approved tenant incentive scheme” means a scheme which is—
-- src:2543 | (a) operated by a provider of social housing and designed to avoid rent arrears by allowing reductions in rent or service charges or other advantages in return for meeting specified conditions; and
-- src:2544 | (b) approved by the Secretary of State.
@ref Sch 4 paras 31, 32 and 32A (src:2531-2544)
DECLARE `Relevant payment in the social rented sector` HAS
    liability                                                                                                           IS A `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
    `amount of the reduction applied by a provider of social housing under a tenant incentive scheme`                  IS A NUMBER
    scheme                                                                                                              IS A `Tenant incentive scheme`
    `amount which the Secretary of State is satisfied is included in the relevant payment and relates to the supply to the accommodation of a commodity (such as water or fuel) for use by a member of the renter's extended benefit unit`  IS A NUMBER
    `a rent officer has determined that a landlord might, at the time of the application, reasonably have expected to obtain a lower amount of the description of relevant payment referred to the rent officer`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lower amount determined by the rent officer`                                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is not appropriate to use the lower amount`                           IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2541 | (1) Where a reduction in the rent or service charge payments for which a renter would otherwise have been liable is applied by a provider of social housing under an approved tenant incentive scheme, the amount of any relevant payment to be taken into account under paragraph 6 is to be determined as if no such reduction had been applied.
@ref Sch 4 para 32A(1) (src:2541)
GIVEN payment IS A `Relevant payment in the social rented sector`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 32A(1) — the amount of the payment determined as if no reduction had been applied` payment MEANS
    ((payment's liability)'s `amount of each payment in pounds`)
    PLUS (IF `Sch 4 para 32A(2) — an approved tenant incentive scheme` (payment's scheme) THEN payment's `amount of the reduction applied by a provider of social housing under a tenant incentive scheme` ELSE 0)

-- src:2532 | In determining the amount of any relevant payment to be taken into account under paragraph 6, a deduction is to be made for any amount which the Secretary of State is satisfied—
-- src:2533 | (a) is included in the relevant payment; but
-- src:2534 | (b) relates to the supply to the accommodation of a commodity (such as water or fuel) for use by any member of the renter's extended benefit unit.
@ref Sch 4 para 31 (src:2532-2534)
GIVEN payment IS A `Relevant payment in the social rented sector`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 31 — the amount of the payment after the deduction for a commodity` payment MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 32A(1) — the amount of the payment determined as if no reduction had been applied` payment)
    MINUS (payment's `amount which the Secretary of State is satisfied is included in the relevant payment and relates to the supply to the accommodation of a commodity (such as water or fuel) for use by a member of the renter's extended benefit unit`)

-- src:2538 | (3) Sub-paragraph (4) applies in any case where a rent officer determines that a landlord might, at the time of the application under sub-paragraph (2), reasonably have expected to obtain a lower amount of the description of relevant payment referred to the rent officer.
-- src:2539 | (4) The lower amount determined by the rent officer is to be used in making the calculation under this Part, instead of the amount of the relevant payment for which the renter is liable, unless the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is not appropriate to use that lower amount.
@ref Sch 4 para 32(3) and (4) (src:2538-2539)
GIVEN payment IS A `Relevant payment in the social rented sector`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 32(4) — the rent officer's lower amount is used` payment MEANS
    (payment's `a rent officer has determined that a landlord might, at the time of the application, reasonably have expected to obtain a lower amount of the description of relevant payment referred to the rent officer`)
    AND (NOT (payment's `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is not appropriate to use the lower amount`))

-- Paragraph 34 Step 1: the amount of the payment to be taken into account.
-- src:2554 | Step 1
-- src:2555 | Determine which relevant payments are to be taken into account under paragraph 6 and determine the amount of each of them (applying paragraphs 31 and 32(3) and (4) as necessary).
@ref Sch 4 para 34 Step 1 (src:2554-2555)
GIVEN payment IS A `Relevant payment in the social rented sector`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 34 Step 1 — the amount of a relevant payment to be taken into account` payment MEANS
    IF `Sch 4 para 32(4) — the rent officer's lower amount is used` payment
    THEN payment's `the lower amount determined by the rent officer`
    ELSE `Sch 4 para 31 — the amount of the payment after the deduction for a commodity` payment

-- Paragraph 34 Step 2: its monthly amount, if it is brought into account under paragraph 6.
-- src:2556 | Step 2
-- src:2557 | Determine the period in respect of which each relevant payment is payable and, in accordance with paragraph 7, determine the amount of the payment in respect of a month.
@ref Sch 4 para 34 Step 2 (src:2556-2557)
GIVEN payment IS A `Relevant payment in the social rented sector`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 34 Step 2 — the monthly amount of a relevant payment` payment MEANS
    IF `Sch 4 para 6 — the liability is brought into account` (payment's liability)
    THEN `Sch 4 para 7 — the monthly equivalent of an amount` (`Sch 4 para 34 Step 1 — the amount of a relevant payment to be taken into account` payment) ((payment's liability)'s `how often the payment falls due`) ((payment's liability)'s `the arrangements provide for one or more rent free periods`) ((payment's liability)'s `total number of the relevant payments which the renter is liable to make in that 12 month period`)
    ELSE 0

-- src:2558 | Step 3
-- src:2559 | If there is more than one relevant payment, add together the amounts determined in step 2 in relation to all relevant payments.
@ref Sch 4 para 34 Step 3 (src:2558-2559)
GIVEN payments IS A LIST OF `Relevant payment in the social rented sector`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 34 Step 3 — the total monthly amount of the relevant payments` payments MEANS
    sum (map `Sch 4 para 34 Step 2 — the monthly amount of a relevant payment` payments)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 36: the under-occupation deduction.
-- src:2584 | (1) A deduction for under-occupancy is to be made under this paragraph where the number of bedrooms in the accommodation exceeds the number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12.
@ref Sch 4 para 36(1) (src:2584)
DECLARE `Facts for the under-occupation deduction` HAS
    `number of bedrooms in the accommodation`                                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership) applies`                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `domestic violence has been inflicted upon or threatened against the claimant or a member of the claimant's extended benefit unit by that person's partner or former partner, or by a relative`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim is not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the domestic violence`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person is a qualifying young person and is a dependant of a member of the claimant's extended benefit unit`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 98(4) (piece uc4), "person acting in an official capacity"
    `the claimant provides evidence from a person acting in an official capacity, within the meaning of regulation 98(4), which demonstrates that the claimant is living in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the scheme is a scheme operated by a provider of social housing enabling victims of domestic violence to remain in their homes through the installation of additional security to the property or the perimeter of the property at which the victim resides`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim's circumstances are consistent with those of a person who has had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity in relation to such an incident`       IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2595 | (6) (a) No deduction for under occupation is to be made in calculating the amount of a renter’s housing cost element under this part where—
-- src:2596 | (i) domestic violence has been inflicted upon or threatened against the claimant or a member of the claimant’s extended benefit unit (“the victim”) by that person’s partner or former partner, or by a relative;
-- src:2597 | (ii) the victim is not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the domestic violence, except where that person is a qualifying young person and is a dependant of a member of the claimant’s extended benefit unit; and
-- src:2598 | (iii) the claimant provides evidence from a person acting in an official capacity which demonstrates that the claimant is living in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme and—
-- src:2599 | (aa) the victim’s circumstances are consistent with those of a person who has had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them; and
-- src:2600 | (bb) the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity in relation to such an incident;
-- src:2601 | (b) in this paragraph—
-- src:2602 | “person acting in an official capacity” has the meaning given to it in regulation 98(4) of these Regulations;
-- src:2604 | “sanctuary scheme” means a scheme operated by a provider of social housing enabling victims of domestic violence to remain in their homes through the installation of additional security to the property or the perimeter of the property at which the victim resides.
@ref Sch 4 para 36(6) (src:2595-2602) (src:2604)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the under-occupation deduction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 36(6) — no deduction is made because of domestic violence and a sanctuary scheme` facts MEANS
    (facts's `domestic violence has been inflicted upon or threatened against the claimant or a member of the claimant's extended benefit unit by that person's partner or former partner, or by a relative`)
    AND (    (facts's `the victim is not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the domestic violence`)
          OR (facts's `that person is a qualifying young person and is a dependant of a member of the claimant's extended benefit unit`))
    AND (facts's `the claimant provides evidence from a person acting in an official capacity, within the meaning of regulation 98(4), which demonstrates that the claimant is living in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme`)
    AND (facts's `the scheme is a scheme operated by a provider of social housing enabling victims of domestic violence to remain in their homes through the installation of additional security to the property or the perimeter of the property at which the victim resides`)
    AND (facts's `the victim's circumstances are consistent with those of a person who has had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them`)
    AND (facts's `the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity in relation to such an incident`)

-- src:2584 | (1) A deduction for under-occupancy is to be made under this paragraph where the number of bedrooms in the accommodation exceeds the number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12.
@ref Sch 4 para 36(1) (src:2584)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the under-occupation deduction`
      `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 36 — the number of excess bedrooms` facts `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12` MEANS
    max 0 ((facts's `number of bedrooms in the accommodation`) MINUS `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12`)

-- src:2592 | (3) The relevant percentage is 14% in the case of one excess bedroom.
-- src:2593 | (4) The relevant percentage is 25% in the case of two or more excess bedrooms.
@ref Sch 4 para 36(3) and (4) (src:2592-2593)
GIVEN `number of excess bedrooms` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 36(3) and (4) — the relevant percentage` `number of excess bedrooms` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `number of excess bedrooms` AT LEAST 2 THEN 25%
        IF `number of excess bedrooms` EQUALS 1 THEN 14%
        OTHERWISE 0

-- src:2584 | (1) A deduction for under-occupancy is to be made under this paragraph where the number of bedrooms in the accommodation exceeds the number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12.
-- src:2585 | (2) Where a deduction is to be made, the amount of the deduction is to be determined by the formula—
-- src:2586 | [formula: A x B]
-- src:2587 | where—
-- src:2588 | “A”—
-- src:2589 | (a) in relation to any deduction under paragraph 34, is the amount resulting from step 2 or 3 in that paragraph (as the case may be), or
-- src:2590 | (b) in relation to any deduction under paragraph 35(3), is the amount resulting from step 3 in paragraph 35(2);
-- src:2591 | “B” is the relevant percentage.
-- src:2592 | (3) The relevant percentage is 14% in the case of one excess bedroom.
-- src:2593 | (4) The relevant percentage is 25% in the case of two or more excess bedrooms.
-- src:2594 | (5) No deduction for under-occupation is to be made in calculating the amount of the renter's housing costs element under this Part in any case to which regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership) applies.
@ref Sch 4 para 36(1) and (5) (src:2584) (src:2594)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the under-occupation deduction`
      `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 36(1) — a deduction for under-occupation is to be made` facts `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12` MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 36 — the number of excess bedrooms` facts `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12` AT LEAST 1)
    AND (NOT (facts's `regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership) applies`))
    AND (NOT (`Sch 4 para 36(6) — no deduction is made because of domestic violence and a sanctuary scheme` facts))

-- src:2585 | (2) Where a deduction is to be made, the amount of the deduction is to be determined by the formula—
-- src:2586 | [formula: A x B]
-- src:2587 | where—
-- src:2588 | “A”—
-- src:2589 | (a) in relation to any deduction under paragraph 34, is the amount resulting from step 2 or 3 in that paragraph (as the case may be), or
-- src:2590 | (b) in relation to any deduction under paragraph 35(3), is the amount resulting from step 3 in paragraph 35(2);
-- src:2591 | “B” is the relevant percentage.
@ref Sch 4 para 36(2) (src:2585-2591)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the under-occupation deduction`
      `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12` IS A NUMBER
      `amount A` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 36(2) — the amount of the under-occupation deduction` facts `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12` `amount A` MEANS
    IF `Sch 4 para 36(1) — a deduction for under-occupation is to be made` facts `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12`
    THEN `amount A` TIMES (`Sch 4 para 36(3) and (4) — the relevant percentage` (`Sch 4 para 36 — the number of excess bedrooms` facts `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12`))
    ELSE 0

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 34: amount S for a renter who is alone liable: the total monthly amount, less the under-occupation deduction (Steps 3 and 4).
-- src:2552 | 34 Determining the amount from which HCC deductions are to be made
-- src:2553 | Except where paragraph 35 applies, amount S referred to in paragraph 33 is to be found as follows.
-- src:2554 | Step 1
-- src:2555 | Determine which relevant payments are to be taken into account under paragraph 6 and determine the amount of each of them (applying paragraphs 31 and 32(3) and (4) as necessary).
-- src:2556 | Step 2
-- src:2557 | Determine the period in respect of which each relevant payment is payable and, in accordance with paragraph 7, determine the amount of the payment in respect of a month.
-- src:2558 | Step 3
-- src:2559 | If there is more than one relevant payment, add together the amounts determined in step 2 in relation to all relevant payments.
-- src:2560 | Step 4
-- src:2561 | Determine under paragraph 36(1) whether an under-occupation deduction is to be made and, if one is to be made, determine the amount of the deduction under paragraph 36(2) and deduct it from the amount resulting from step 2 or 3 (as the case may be).
-- src:2562 | The result is amount S from which the sum of the housing costs contributions are to be deducted under paragraph 33.
@ref Sch 4 para 34 (src:2552-2562)
GIVEN payments IS A LIST OF `Relevant payment in the social rented sector`
      facts IS A `Facts for the under-occupation deduction`
      `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 34 — amount S` payments facts `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12` MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 34 Step 3 — the total monthly amount of the relevant payments` payments)
    MINUS (`Sch 4 para 36(2) — the amount of the under-occupation deduction` facts `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12` (`Sch 4 para 34 Step 3 — the total monthly amount of the relevant payments` payments))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 35: joint tenants. Step 3 total; then (3) only listed persons liable: the total less the under-occupation deduction; (4) listed and other
-- persons liable: (A/B) x C, with no under-occupation deduction (fork U3-F22); (5) the Secretary of State's allocation if (4) would be unreasonable.
-- src:2564 | (1) This paragraph applies where, in respect of the accommodation occupied by the renter, one or more persons other than the renter is liable to make relevant payments which are of the same description as those for which the renter is liable and which are to be taken into account under paragraph 6.
-- src:2565 | (2) Amount S referred to in paragraph 33 is to be found as follows.
-- src:2566 | Step 1
-- src:2567 | Determine the total of all relevant payments referred to in sub-paragraph (1) for which the renter and others are liable in respect of the accommodation taken as a whole (applying paragraphs 31 and 32(3) and (4) as necessary).
-- src:2568 | Step 2
-- src:2569 | Determine the period in respect of which each relevant payment is payable and, in accordance with paragraph 7, determine the amount of the payment in respect of a month.
-- src:2570 | Step 3
-- src:2571 | Add together all of the amounts determined in step 2 in relation to all relevant payments.
-- src:2572 | Step 4
-- src:2573 | Find amount S in accordance with whichever of sub-paragraphs (3) to (5) applies in the renter's case.
-- src:2574 | The result is amount S from which the sum of the housing costs contributions are to be deducted under paragraph 33.
@ref Sch 4 para 35(1) and (2) (src:2564-2574)
DECLARE `Joint liability in the social rented sector` HAS
    `relevant payments of the renter and of the others in respect of the accommodation taken as a whole`  IS A LIST OF `Relevant payment in the social rented sector`
    `number of listed persons liable to make relevant payments`                                          IS A NUMBER
    `number of other persons liable to make relevant payments`                                           IS A NUMBER
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to determine amount S in accordance with sub-paragraph (4)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount S determined in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate in all the circumstances`  IS A NUMBER

-- src:2576 | (4) Where the persons liable for the relevant payments are one or more listed persons and one or more other persons, amount S is to be found by the applying the formula—
-- src:2577 | [formula: ( (A)/(B) ) x C]
-- src:2578 | where—
-- src:2579 | “A” is the amount resulting from step 3 in sub-paragraph (2),
-- src:2580 | “B” is the total number of all persons (including listed persons) liable to make the relevant payments, and
-- src:2581 | “C” is the number of listed persons liable to make relevant payments.
@ref Sch 4 para 35(4) (src:2576-2581)
GIVEN joint IS A `Joint liability in the social rented sector`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 35(4) — amount S by the formula` joint MEANS
    ((`Sch 4 para 34 Step 3 — the total monthly amount of the relevant payments` (joint's `relevant payments of the renter and of the others in respect of the accommodation taken as a whole`)) DIVIDED BY ((joint's `number of listed persons liable to make relevant payments`) PLUS (joint's `number of other persons liable to make relevant payments`))) TIMES (joint's `number of listed persons liable to make relevant payments`)

-- src:2563 | 35 Determining the amount from which HCC deductions are to be made: joint tenants
-- src:2564 | (1) This paragraph applies where, in respect of the accommodation occupied by the renter, one or more persons other than the renter is liable to make relevant payments which are of the same description as those for which the renter is liable and which are to be taken into account under paragraph 6.
-- src:2565 | (2) Amount S referred to in paragraph 33 is to be found as follows.
-- src:2566 | Step 1
-- src:2567 | Determine the total of all relevant payments referred to in sub-paragraph (1) for which the renter and others are liable in respect of the accommodation taken as a whole (applying paragraphs 31 and 32(3) and (4) as necessary).
-- src:2568 | Step 2
-- src:2569 | Determine the period in respect of which each relevant payment is payable and, in accordance with paragraph 7, determine the amount of the payment in respect of a month.
-- src:2570 | Step 3
-- src:2571 | Add together all of the amounts determined in step 2 in relation to all relevant payments.
-- src:2572 | Step 4
-- src:2573 | Find amount S in accordance with whichever of sub-paragraphs (3) to (5) applies in the renter's case.
-- src:2574 | The result is amount S from which the sum of the housing costs contributions are to be deducted under paragraph 33.
-- src:2575 | (3) Where the only persons liable to make relevant payments are listed persons, amount S is the amount resulting from step 3 in sub-paragraph (2) less the amount of the under-occupation deduction (if any) required by paragraph 36.
-- src:2576 | (4) Where the persons liable for the relevant payments are one or more listed persons and one or more other persons, amount S is to be found by the applying the formula—
-- src:2577 | [formula: ( (A)/(B) ) x C]
-- src:2578 | where—
-- src:2579 | “A” is the amount resulting from step 3 in sub-paragraph (2),
-- src:2580 | “B” is the total number of all persons (including listed persons) liable to make the relevant payments, and
-- src:2581 | “C” is the number of listed persons liable to make relevant payments.
-- src:2582 | (5) If the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to determine amount S in accordance with sub-paragraph (4), amount S is to be determined in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate in all the circumstances, having regard (among other things) to the number of persons liable and the proportion of the relevant payments for which each of them is liable.
@ref Sch 4 para 35 (src:2563-2582)
GIVEN joint IS A `Joint liability in the social rented sector`
      facts IS A `Facts for the under-occupation deduction`
      `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 35 — amount S for joint tenants` joint facts `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (joint's `number of other persons liable to make relevant payments`) EQUALS 0 THEN `Sch 4 para 34 — amount S` (joint's `relevant payments of the renter and of the others in respect of the accommodation taken as a whole`) facts `number of bedrooms to which the renter is entitled under paragraphs 8 to 12`
        IF joint's `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to determine amount S in accordance with sub-paragraph (4)` THEN joint's `amount S determined in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate in all the circumstances`
        OTHERWISE `Sch 4 para 35(4) — amount S by the formula` joint

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 33: S less the housing cost contributions; not below nil (paragraph 14(3)).
-- src:2546 | 33 The amount of housing costs element
-- src:2547 | The amount of the renter's housing costs element under this Part is to be calculated by reference to the formula—
-- src:2548 | [formula: S − H C C]
-- src:2549 | where—
-- src:2550 | “S” is the amount resulting from whichever of paragraph 34 or 35 applies in the renter's case, and
-- src:2551 | “HCC” is the sum of the housing cost contributions (if any) under paragraph 13.
@ref Sch 4 para 33 (src:2546-2551)
GIVEN `amount S` IS A NUMBER
      `sum of the housing cost contributions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 33 — the amount of the renter's housing costs element under Part 5` `amount S` `sum of the housing cost contributions` MEANS
    `Sch 4 para 14(2) and (3)(a) — the amount after the housing cost contributions are deducted` `amount S` `sum of the housing cost contributions`
